.SH DURABLE EVENTS
.B doorman events --json
reads a page from the optional SQLite event journal, through an internal
public_events_v1 view. No public SQL access or HTTP service is required.
.TP
.B --after cursor
Exclusive sequence cursor. Default 0 explicitly starts at the earliest
retained event.
.TP
.B --through cursor
Inclusive upper cursor; reuse the returned through value to finish a finite
batch.
.TP
.B --direction direction, --line name, --call id
Filter by inbound/outbound direction, line, or full channel ID.
.TP
.B --limit count
Maximum returned events, 1 to 10000; default 100.
.TP
.B --eventType type
One exact event type, or omitted for all. See --help for the enum.
.TP
.B --path file
Override EVENT_JOURNAL_PATH (environment, then .env).
.TP
.B --no-redact
Explicitly export full phone numbers. PINs and entered digits are never stored.
.TP
.B --journal id, --generation id
Assert the identity saved alongside the consumer cursor.
.PP
Output is one JSON object containing events, next_cursor, earliest_available,
high_watermark, through, retention_floor, journal_id and generation. Cursors
are decimal
strings. Save progress only after successful processing. Expired cursors and
identity mismatches fail rather than silently skipping history.
.PP
EVENT_JOURNAL_PATH enables storage in a private 0700 directory. Defaults are
EVENT_JOURNAL_MAX_BYTES=67108864, EVENT_JOURNAL_MAX_EVENTS=100000 and
EVENT_JOURNAL_MAX_AGE_DAYS=90. Storage failure never delays calls; it degrades
observation and is reported. Only committed events are durable.
.PP
WEBHOOK_MODE defaults to legacy. Set doorbell to announce committed journal
availability through WEBHOOK_URL, using WEBHOOK_TOKEN and WEBHOOK_TIMEOUT_MS.
Doorbells contain no call payload. Consumers retrieve their own batches and
check periodically as well as on notifications. Doorbell mode requires a
journal.
.PP
doorman calls reads completed-session summaries from the journal when
configured,
preserving its table and JSON Lines formats. The daemon writes CALL_LOG_PATH
only when the journal is disabled. Use --source jsonl to read old files
explicitly;
--source auto prefers the journal and never silently falls back on a read error.
Summaries share journal retention; use the events command for consumer replay.
.PP
CEL_SPOOL_PATH enables Asterisk-wide lifecycle capture from a private SQLite CEL
spool initialised with scripts/cel-spool.sql. It requires EVENT_JOURNAL_PATH.
Install the supplied CEL configs, verify backend status, and validate with
doorman check. Source progress and events commit together. A session finish
or handoff is not proof the call ended. See docs/events.md for the full
contract.

.PP
The default byte budget permits 16 MiB of database pages, often binding before
count or age: roughly 27000 mixed events, workload dependent, not guaranteed
90-day retention. Size storage for the consumer outage window.
.PP
Reinstall the supplied systemd unit on upgrade for StateDirectory support.
An explicitly configured journal must open at startup; runtime failures remain
nonfatal to calls. check --policy-only skips local service environment/storage
checks when validating examples.
Normal check reports policy before environment.

.SH LOCAL GAME PREVIEW
.B doorman games check|serve --pack DIR --handsets FILE --rooms id,id
validates or runs an opt-in Starlark game on selected internal handsets.
The separate doorman-games-preview ARI application supports accepted room
invitations.
See docs/GAME-PREVIEW.md for installation, controls and rollback.

.SH MANAGED WEBHOOK
The optional private webhook.toml beside policy.toml accepts domain (HTTP or
HTTPS origin) and path_prefix. See doorman schema webhook. The daemon POSTs
JSON event payloads to domain + path_prefix + /cc.dialdoorman/events for
ringing and completed calls. Managed delivery redacts caller numbers and
never inherits WEBHOOK_TOKEN. Empty values disable managed delivery; an
absent file preserves the environment default. The separate journal doorbell
is unchanged. Keep this file and its .last-good copy mode 0600. Invalid edits
keep the last good endpoint across restart; doorman check validates the file.
Sync applies encrypted, revision-checked changes and reports applied only
after the running daemon accepts the exact file revision.
.SH PODCAST PILOT
.B doorman schema podcasts
prints the optional handset subscription JSON schema.
.B doorman podcasts check --config file --handsets inventory
checks its shape and handset references.
.B doorman podcasts refresh
prepares two pinned Brains On episodes off the call path;
.B doorman podcasts status
prints readiness separately from subscription sync.
The local *PODS (*7637) AGI shares Opus audio and keeps per-handset bookmarks.
See docs/PODCASTS.md for release installation and a real handset trial.
.SH COMPLETE RECORDED AUDIOBOOKS
.B doorman books install-recorded --archive book.cmmpack
verifies and installs a local recorded audiobook without an account.
.B doorman sync media once --source https://trusted.example --full-books
opts into disk-streamed complete recordings (256 MiB maximum).
Both retain compressed Opus audio and use bounded playback conversion.
Prepared menu voices require a matching offline bundle before catalog
activation;
see docs/media-preview.md for the candidate catalog and --menu-bundle workflow.
